2026-05-30T07:04Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context

A script that pipes `erg list | jq` or captures `erg new` output breaks silently if an error
message leaks to stdout. The convention is: success output to stdout, all diagnostics to stderr.

A source audit of `src/go/*.go` shows all `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, ...)` calls look correct. But
the audit was done by grep — it does not verify that every *error return path* actually reaches
one of those calls. And there is no blackbox pin: removing `os.Stderr` from a `fmt.Fprintf` call
would not be caught by any existing test.

## Part 1 — Source audit

Grep every `fmt.Print*` call (not to `os.Stderr`, not to a file handle) in `src/go/*.go`
(excluding `_test.go`). Each such call is a success-path stdout write — verify it is on the
success path and not reachable from an error branch. Document findings in the commit message.

If any error-path stdout write is found, fix it in the same PR.

## Part 2 — Blackbox pin

For each command that has an error mode (all mutating commands), add a test that:

1. Triggers a known error (e.g. `erg close NONEXISTENT reason DIR`)
2. Captures stdout only (`2>/dev/null`)
3. Asserts stdout is empty

Negative control: the same command with valid arguments produces non-empty stdout (or exits 0
with output), confirming the assertion would fire if the check were reversed.

Commands to cover (error triggers):
- `erg close NONEXISTENT reason DIR` → "no ticket found"
- `erg log NONEXISTENT "line" DIR` → "no ticket found"
- `erg rm NONEXISTENT DIR` → "no ticket found"
- `erg new "" DIR` → "title is required"
- `erg validate /nonexistent.erg` → file not found

Add to `test_main.sh` or a new `test_stderr.sh`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Source audit complete; any error-path stdout writes fixed
- [ ] Blackbox tests added: for each command above, error produces empty stdout
- [ ] Each blackbox test has a paired negative control (valid input → non-empty stdout)
- [ ] `make check` passes
